<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Wen of Zhu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 614 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Wen of Zhu was a ruler of the small state of Zhu, later known as Zou, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>. In 614 BCE he moved the capital to Yi after a divination warned that it would benefit the people but not the ruler, answering that a ruler's task was to benefit the people. He died soon after, and the story was cited as a model of virtue.</p></div>
